WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:08.759
Hi!

00:00:08.759 --> 00:00:13.309
So, you’ve done all the preparation and
practised your English a lot, and now you

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:16.369
want to know what you can do during the exam.

00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:20.780
Here are five tips to help you get the best
mark in your next speaking exam.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:28.740
Number one: Remember, it’s not a race - so slow down!

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:34.660
Before you speak, think carefully about what you want to say and speak a little slower than normal.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:43.690
Number two: If you don’t understand the
question or the activity, don’t worry.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.199
Ask the examiner to explain it again.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.060
You can say something like,‘Could you repeat
that, please?’

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:58.559
Number three: When you’re asked a question, don’t just say ‘yes’ or ‘no’ as

00:00:58.559 --> 00:00:59.760
your answer.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.559
The examiner wants to know how good your English is!

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:05.500
So, try to explain your answer with a reason.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.840
Say ‘Yes, I agree because ...’ or ‘No,
I don’t think so, because …’

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:21.960
Number four: Look at the examiner’s or other students’ faces and eyes when you speak.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.220
Faces can tell you a lot!

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.590
If you see that the examiner or your partner
don’t understand you, then say it again

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.480
using different words.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:37.660
And finally number five: Speak clearly so
that the examiner can hear you.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.680
If you find this difficult, practise with
a friend at home.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.530
Stand at opposite ends of a room and speak to each other in English.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.000
Or speak to each other in English online or on the phone.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.840
OK - so these are our top five tips - but
just one final piece of advice.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.020
Your teacher or examiner are only human - and usually they will really want you to do well.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:08.240
So, take a deep breath, smile, relax and …. good luck with your next speaking exam!

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.640
For more tips on learning English, why not
subscribe to our channel and visit the LearnEnglish

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.030
Teens Website for more learning material!

